(2344527, 325005, 31349, '<td valign="top">Nice.  Where is this?</td>', 'Nice.  Where is this?', '2006-04-26 04:09:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(2344540, 323686, 31349, '<td valign="top">Clever.  I would like to have seen the heads of the people.  It would have added greater tension to the picture -  a simultaneous feeling of detachment from people yet a yearning for a connection by the act of looking at them. .</td>', 'Clever.  I would like to have seen the heads of the people.  It would have added greater tension to the picture -  a simultaneous feeling of detachment from people yet a yearning for a connection by the act of looking at them. .', '2006-04-26 04:16:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(2344541, 325134, 31349, '<td valign="top">Do those ruby slippers belong to the WIcked Witch of the West?  My how she''s changed.</td>', 'Do those ruby slippers belong to the WIcked Witch of the West?  My how she''s changed.', '2006-04-26 04:17:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(2344911, 324657, 51875, '<td valign="top">Great angle, really good idea and the textures on the walls on the sides are really cool!</td>', 'Great angle, really good idea and the textures on the walls on the sides are really cool!', '2006-04-26 06:56:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(2344964, 323708, 30364, '<td valign="top">Remarkable for a "from-the-hip" type candid that you could achieve the level of concentration or focus (in the non-photographic sense) that you have here.  This photograph is all about one person, but it''s a person in context; a context that every component of the photograph serves.  It''s as if you took an hour to set it up, and yet it was no doubt just a heartbeat!  Admirable, instructive work.  9.</td>', 'Remarkable for a "from-the-hip" type candid that you could achieve the level of concentration or focus (in the non-photographic sense) that you have here.  This photograph is all about one person, but it''s a person in context; a context that every component of the photograph serves.  It''s as if you took an hour to set it up, and yet it was no doubt just a heartbeat!  Admirable, instructive work.  9.', '2006-04-26 07:08:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(2344965, 324110, 8610, '<td valign="top">Woowww,, this Idea is awesome. This will be in top 20 for sure</td>', 'Woowww,, this Idea is awesome. This will be in top 20 for sure', '2006-04-26 07:08:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(2345010, 325114, 30364, '<td valign="top">This is very, very good.  Framed <i>by</i> windows!  So refreshing to see an image that''s not a slave to tedious bloody literalism.  And it''s an interesting, ambitious image, too.  Not content with thumbing your nose at the DNMC literalists, you say "screw you" to the composition police as well.  <i>How do I love the?  Let me count the ways! (EBB)</i> 9.</td>', 'This is very, very good.  Framed by windows!  So refreshing to see an image that''s not a slave to tedious bloody literalism.  And it''s an interesting, ambitious image, too.  Not content with thumbing your nose at the DNMC literalists, you say "screw you" to the composition police as well.  How do I love the?  Let me count the ways! (EBB) 9.', '2006-04-26 07:16:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(2345403, 324421, 30364, '<td valign="top">Great location!  Very fine use of light, very fine control of tone, and really terrific composition.  Also nice to see the idea of "window framed" interpreted with some subtlety, rather than as an overly-literal smack in the head.  <br/>I can''t avoid seeing this man as a prison minister or priest.  And it''s not just his stance with bowed head ... it''s that you have managed to suggest an unexpected cathedral in this location, complete with soaring stained-glass windows!  So he must be a man of God, musn''t he?  <br/>It''s one of the two best and most thoughtful images in the challenge <i>(other one''s called Bored on a Rainy Day).</i> <br/>I''ll give it a 10 (which is no favour; a 10 from me is inevitably the kiss of death ... sorry!)</td>', 'Great location!  Very fine use of light, very fine control of tone, and really terrific composition.  Also nice to see the idea of "window framed" interpreted with some subtlety, rather than as an overly-literal smack in the head.  I can''t avoid seeing this man as a prison minister or priest.  And it''s not just his stance with bowed head ... it''s that you have managed to suggest an unexpected cathedral in this location, complete with soaring stained-glass windows!  So he must be a man of God, musn''t he?  It''s one of the two best and most thoughtful images in the challenge (other one''s called Bored on a Rainy Day). I''ll give it a 10 (which is no favour; a 10 from me is inevitably the kiss of death ... sorry!)', '2006-04-26 08:37:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(2345463, 323806, 10702, '<td valign="top">Haha<br/> <br/>góður !</td>', 'Haha góður !', '2006-04-26 08:47:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(2345471, 325118, 30364, '<td valign="top">I loved cigars, back when I smoked.  I can smell these still.<br/>But there''s a lot more to love here than memories.  Very interesting &amp; effective use of the window frame motif; great character in the tattoo and the earring; nice visual complexity in the reflected (?) secondary subject.  There''s something both comfortable and comforting about this photograph .. as if they are quietly saying "screw fashion and convention; we smoke cigars."  Or you''re saying it for them, which is even more pleasing.  8.</td>', 'I loved cigars, back when I smoked.  I can smell these still.But there''s a lot more to love here than memories.  Very interesting & effective use of the window frame motif; great character in the tattoo and the earring; nice visual complexity in the reflected (?) secondary subject.  There''s something both comfortable and comforting about this photograph .. as if they are quietly saying "screw fashion and convention; we smoke cigars."  Or you''re saying it for them, which is even more pleasing.  8.', '2006-04-26 08:50:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(2345481, 323897, 30364, '<td valign="top">Simple idea, but really terrific composition.  I''ve always been a composition man.  7.</td>', 'Simple idea, but really terrific composition.  I''ve always been a composition man.  7.', '2006-04-26 08:53:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(2345521, 325094, 30364, '<td valign="top">This has got all sorts of brutal sharpening halos, and I don''t care at all.  I like the whacky, interesting composition, and I like the effect created by the processing artifacts ... as if the image is created by "cut-out" primary components, but balanced with beautifully subtle secondary details (sky and city background).  Bold and pleasing.  8.</td>', 'This has got all sorts of brutal sharpening halos, and I don''t care at all.  I like the whacky, interesting composition, and I like the effect created by the processing artifacts ... as if the image is created by "cut-out" primary components, but balanced with beautifully subtle secondary details (sky and city background).  Bold and pleasing.  8.', '2006-04-26 09:00:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(2345557, 324784, 30364, '<td valign="top">One of very few literally framed images to have any real point to it.  The window serves a worthy purpose here, by creating a natural polyptych ... it could be the woman; her memories; her fears; her <i>alter ego.</i>   Other interesting quadratic interpretations are possible.  Either way, the window framing seems natural and an important part of the meaning of the photograph.  8.</td>', 'One of very few literally framed images to have any real point to it.  The window serves a worthy purpose here, by creating a natural polyptych ... it could be the woman; her memories; her fears; her alter ego.   Other interesting quadratic interpretations are possible.  Either way, the window framing seems natural and an important part of the meaning of the photograph.  8.', '2006-04-26 09:10:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(2345576, 323551, 30364, '<td valign="top">Maybe a little bit sentimental for my taste (I wouldn''t put Norman Rockwell on a biscuit tin), but it is beautifully executed and I especially like the creative use of the window frame to enhance and amplify the image rather than merely to crudely enclose it.  7.</td>', 'Maybe a little bit sentimental for my taste (I wouldn''t put Norman Rockwell on a biscuit tin), but it is beautifully executed and I especially like the creative use of the window frame to enhance and amplify the image rather than merely to crudely enclose it.  7.', '2006-04-26 09:18:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(2345588, 324747, 30364, '<td valign="top">I can never resist taking these in-flight shots, but mine seldom look any good.  Yours does.  Approaching home, or perhaps arriving at a new place; either way it''s an exciting experience and your photograph captures that feeling well.  Of course, the rainbow makes it even more interesting.  7.</td>', 'I can never resist taking these in-flight shots, but mine seldom look any good.  Yours does.  Approaching home, or perhaps arriving at a new place; either way it''s an exciting experience and your photograph captures that feeling well.  Of course, the rainbow makes it even more interesting.  7.', '2006-04-26 09:24:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(2345656, 323806, 31443, '<td valign="top">Wow! Must be Iceland!</td>', 'Wow! Must be Iceland!', '2006-04-26 09:47:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(2346127, 324890, 56658, '<td valign="top">I like it but the glare(or shadows) really detracts from it.</td>', 'I like it but the glare(or shadows) really detracts from it.', '2006-04-26 12:24:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(2346150, 325012, 56658, '<td valign="top">If the bird is alive then great capturebut i have a feeling he is not. either way nice subject. I like the image overall but it has some graininess to it. maybe the screen ahould have been taken off.</td>', 'If the bird is alive then great capturebut i have a feeling he is not. either way nice subject. I like the image overall but it has some graininess to it. maybe the screen ahould have been taken off.', '2006-04-26 12:30:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(2346198, 324993, 38032, '<td valign="top">I love this one.  I like that you chose to have the models look at the camera. Really nice and a refreshing idea. 8</td>', 'I love this one.  I like that you chose to have the models look at the camera. Really nice and a refreshing idea. 8', '2006-04-26 12:40:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(2346202, 324816, 56658, '<td valign="top">I would like it more if the sillouete (sp?) were black. also i think you could have cut off the top row of frames</td>', 'I would like it more if the sillouete (sp?) were black. also i think you could have cut off the top row of frames', '2006-04-26 12:41:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(2346218, 324902, 50640, '<td valign="top">I like this, but I think it may be underexposed, or maybe there is a problem with white balance. (Rookie trying to comment here!). But it is neat. Good luck.</td>', 'I like this, but I think it may be underexposed, or maybe there is a problem with white balance. (Rookie trying to comment here!). But it is neat. Good luck.', '2006-04-26 12:45:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(2346222, 324838, 50640, '<td valign="top">It seems a little too blue/green. I love the figure on the bridge--would cropping have helped bring that out more? (If that''s what you''re after.) Good luck.</td>', 'It seems a little too blue/green. I love the figure on the bridge--would cropping have helped bring that out more? (If that''s what you''re after.) Good luck.', '2006-04-26 12:47:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(2346230, 324856, 57886, '<td valign="top">Nice shot... Good flying :o)</td>', 'Nice shot... Good flying :o)', '2006-04-26 12:49:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(2346232, 323522, 56658, '<td valign="top">nice but would look better (to me) if the window lines were level</td>', 'nice but would look better (to me) if the window lines were level', '2006-04-26 12:51:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(2346237, 324792, 57886, '<td valign="top">Like this photo alot, nice serious face...</td>', 'Like this photo alot, nice serious face...', '2006-04-26 12:52:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(2346239, 324972, 56658, '<td valign="top">I would like to see less of the border</td>', 'I would like to see less of the border', '2006-04-26 12:53:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(2346271, 323686, 49007, '<td valign="top">The subject seems to be the WINDOW vs. the window FRAMING THE SUBJECT.</td>', 'The subject seems to be the WINDOW vs. the window FRAMING THE SUBJECT.', '2006-04-26 13:01:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(2346338, 324541, 19944, '<td valign="top">The subject is very sharp through the window.  Some of your highlights are just a bit blown out.  I personally would have cropped a little more at top &amp; bottom to get rid of the edges of those panes.  i really like the layout on this.  Almost like a painting.</td>', 'The subject is very sharp through the window.  Some of your highlights are just a bit blown out.  I personally would have cropped a little more at top & bottom to get rid of the edges of those panes.  i really like the layout on this.  Almost like a painting.', '2006-04-26 13:17:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(2346347, 324980, 19944, '<td valign="top">I like this.  It''s busy, but also minimalist in a way.  My only gripe would be that the top is thicker than at the bottom and is a little distracting to me.</td>', 'I like this.  It''s busy, but also minimalist in a way.  My only gripe would be that the top is thicker than at the bottom and is a little distracting to me.', '2006-04-26 13:18:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(2346351, 323234, 19944, '<td valign="top">I am assuming that this is a reflection.  Very good capture.  Great color, and I like thehout of focus door handles.</td>', 'I am assuming that this is a reflection.  Very good capture.  Great color, and I like thehout of focus door handles.', '2006-04-26 13:20:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(2346361, 324076, 19944, '<td valign="top">I like the desat, but wish the flowers were just a little sharper.  Otherwise, I think this is excellent.</td>', 'I like the desat, but wish the flowers were just a little sharper.  Otherwise, I think this is excellent.', '2006-04-26 13:23:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(2346400, 325075, 56658, '<td valign="top">those chickens have a nice view.</td>', 'those chickens have a nice view.', '2006-04-26 13:32:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(2346613, 324139, 38198, '<td valign="top">Nice shot love the light</td>', 'Nice shot love the light', '2006-04-26 14:21:23.000000', NULL, 1),
