(2351159, 325020, 6999, '<td valign="top">I think, as far as this place is concerned, images such as this which depend for their effect on the purely graphic are more liked if they have big bright colours. There is something to the relationship of glass and glass here, but perhaps it needs something to emphasise that first layer of glass? Reflections maybe? Just thoughts ...</td>', 'I think, as far as this place is concerned, images such as this which depend for their effect on the purely graphic are more liked if they have big bright colours. There is something to the relationship of glass and glass here, but perhaps it needs something to emphasise that first layer of glass? Reflections maybe? Just thoughts ...', '2006-04-27 17:18:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(2351168, 325139, 56548, '<td valign="top">nice</td>', 'nice', '2006-04-27 17:23:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(2351173, 325079, 40679, '<td valign="top">I really love the idea, but I think adding a little spark into the photo, it would be even better. The branches at the bottom, top and right don''t really add anything to the photo.</td>', 'I really love the idea, but I think adding a little spark into the photo, it would be even better. The branches at the bottom, top and right don''t really add anything to the photo.', '2006-04-27 17:28:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(2351179, 324420, 40679, '<td valign="top">I think this oe could be great if the lighting was better. the inside-walls are a bit too dark, and the 1/2 man is a bit too light. maybe the use of a flash is helpful.</td>', 'I think this oe could be great if the lighting was better. the inside-walls are a bit too dark, and the 1/2 man is a bit too light. maybe the use of a flash is helpful.', '2006-04-27 17:29:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(2351181, 323467, 40679, '<td valign="top">nice framing, I really like the clouds, framed in the top window. looks like the''re painted. bumping to 7 :)</td>', 'nice framing, I really like the clouds, framed in the top window. looks like the''re painted. bumping to 7 :)', '2006-04-27 17:30:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(2351187, 324579, 6999, '<td valign="top">I like this; My own shot plays wth the idea of the two worlds of the refelected and the transmitted light, as does this. You''ve achieved more with the graphic relationship of that reflected world to the direct one though. One thing: I would wish for a more involved treatment of it. This comes across as very much a real world thing; perhaps taking this into the black and white world would emphasise those overlaid views a touch more - in effect, make the photograph be about those conjunctions, rather than the tendency of this to make it more of a portrait. I just neither likie nor understand the idea of the photographic portrait, you understand - it may be, to those who appreciate them, that this is a great one. <br/> <br/>There''s a temporariness about the bed here too - no valance, the shaping of the edge of that ''mattress'' almost makes one think of a sofa-bed, or a guest room. I like that transience - and the complexity of those reflections just add to the absorption of the whole scene. Top work.</td>', 'I like this; My own shot plays wth the idea of the two worlds of the refelected and the transmitted light, as does this. You''ve achieved more with the graphic relationship of that reflected world to the direct one though. One thing: I would wish for a more involved treatment of it. This comes across as very much a real world thing; perhaps taking this into the black and white world would emphasise those overlaid views a touch more - in effect, make the photograph be about those conjunctions, rather than the tendency of this to make it more of a portrait. I just neither likie nor understand the idea of the photographic portrait, you understand - it may be, to those who appreciate them, that this is a great one.  There''s a temporariness about the bed here too - no valance, the shaping of the edge of that ''mattress'' almost makes one think of a sofa-bed, or a guest room. I like that transience - and the complexity of those reflections just add to the absorption of the whole scene. Top work.', '2006-04-27 17:30:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(2351213, 323804, 45360, '<td valign="top">This must get a ribbon!  Love the detail and textures, made me smile.<br/>As it was advanced editing perhaps could have cloned out the cable on this right...<br/>8</td>', 'This must get a ribbon!  Love the detail and textures, made me smile.As it was advanced editing perhaps could have cloned out the cable on this right...8', '2006-04-27 17:35:19.000000', NULL, 1),
