(2367281, 324404, 38509, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Larus:</b></div><hr/><i> Nice view.  I got to question making this duotone, was it really better that way?  Think this could have been so great with a deep blue sky and green hills...  Nice shot though, just my impression was that. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>hi, thanks a lot :-)<br/>do you mean something like this ?<br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=328597" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/38509/thumb/328597.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/38509/thumb/328597.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/38509/thumb/328597.jpg"/></a> <br/> <br/>i decided to ga against it coz colors were washed pretty bad and this one was the best i could pull out, so i stayed with the duotone/vintage look ... and of course the railings are really really hurting my eyes :-) ... but it''s a view to the outside<br/> <br/>thanks again<br/> <br/>g.</td>', 'Originally posted by Larus: Nice view.  I got to question making this duotone, was it really better that way?  Think this could have been so great with a deep blue sky and green hills...  Nice shot though, just my impression was that.   hi, thanks a lot :-)do you mean something like this ?  i decided to ga against it coz colors were washed pretty bad and this one was the best i could pull out, so i stayed with the duotone/vintage look ... and of course the railings are really really hurting my eyes :-) ... but it''s a view to the outside thanks again g.', '2006-05-01 05:47:54.000000', NULL, 0),
