 focus. To grow its vote?: Without details on the shot I can''t say. Summary: You are good at commenting on others shots .. so I was disapointed that you don''t include details on your own which help us all to grow through the critque process. If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via the PM system. Cheers Kari', '2006-05-07 01:31:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(2388641, 324548, 43434, '<td valign="top"><b><i>::: Critique Club :::</i></b> <br/> <br/>Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club.<br/> <br/>Interesting to do a critique on your image but it is difficult if you don''t give us any information in your photographers comments.  When we do a critique, we go past just the photographic result, that''s what voters comments do.  The critique looks at what you were trying to achieve, how you wanted it to look and what issues you had in getting the image captured and ready for voting.<br/> <br/><b>First Impression - the most important one:</b> <br/>personally not big on the doggie cat pics, but this one really works well ... love the reflections which feed us his message.<br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>I like the way the dog seems to lie on the horizontal thirds here .. quite interesting.<br/> <br/><b>Subject:</b> <br/>meets the challenge ... does it ok ... in fact does it really well!<br/> <br/><b>Technical (Colour and light):</b> <br/>It seems a little washed out .. this may be due to the contrast etc ... but I don''t know what you did.<br/> <br/><b>To grow its vote?:</b> <br/>I think that it is finding a subject which appeals to more than one section of the community ... this is a good shot with a solid result.<br/> <br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/> <br/>Good shooting .. you are learning well keep it up!<br/>If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via the PM system.<br/> <br/>Cheers<br/> <br/>Kari</td>', '::: Critique Club :::  Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club. Interesting to do a critique on your image but it is difficult if you don''t give us any information in your photographers comments.  When we do a critique, we go past just the photographic result, that''s what voters comments do.  The critique looks at what you were trying to achieve, how you wanted it to look and what issues you had in getting the image captured and ready for voting. First Impression - the most important one: personally not big on the doggie cat pics, but this one really works well ... love the reflections which feed us his message. Composition: I like the way the dog seems to lie on the horizontal thirds here .. quite interesting. Subject: meets the challenge ... does it ok ... in fact does it really well! Technical (Colour and light): It seems a little washed out .. this may be due to the contrast etc ... but I don''t know what you did. To grow its vote?: I think that it is finding a subject which appeals to more than one section of the community ... this is a good shot with a solid result. Summary:  Good shooting .. you are learning well keep it up!If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via the PM system. Cheers Kari', '2006-05-07 01:35:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(2388651, 325102, 43434, '<td valign="top"><b><i>::: Critique Club :::</i></b> <br/> <br/>Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club.<br/> <br/>Interesting to do a critique on your image but it is difficult if you don''t give us any information in your photographers comments.  When we do a critique, we go past just the photographic result, that''s what voters comments do.  The critique looks at what you were trying to achieve, how you wanted it to look and what issues you had in getting the image captured and ready for voting.<br/> <br/>Now I don''t think you had your one handed keyboard for this shot so can understand not entering comments .. but I know you got it now .. they really do help with critiquing.<br/> <br/><b>First Impression - the most important one:</b> <br/>Interesting shot .. good framing .. nicely out of the box this one.<br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>This is a reasonable though not stunning composition .. this may be due to the selective desat impression ... not sure ...<br/> <br/><b>Subject:</b> <br/>meets the challenge in spades.<br/> <br/><b>Technical (Colour and light):</b> <br/>This is good natural light from the looks ... and I love the DOF ... I am biased on selective desat and think it does work in some cases but it seems a little overkill in this shot ...<br/> <br/><b>To grow its vote?:</b> <br/>I would have loved to have seen this in colour to see how that works ... this I think would make a huge difference to the shot.<br/> <br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>Good shooting .. you are overall improving all the time ...<br/> <br/>If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via the PM system.<br/> <br/>Cheers<br/> <br/>Kari</td>', '::: Critique Club :::  Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club. Interesting to do a critique on your image but it is difficult if you don''t give us any information in your photographers comments.  When we do a critique, we go past just the photographic result, that''s what voters comments do.  The critique looks at what you were trying to achieve, how you wanted it to look and what issues you had in getting the image captured and ready for voting. Now I don''t think you had your one handed keyboard for this shot so can understand not entering comments .. but I know you got it now .. they really do help with critiquing. First Impression - the most important one: Interesting shot .. good framing .. nicely out of the box this one. Composition: This is a reasonable though not stunning composition .. this may be due to the selective desat impression ... not sure ... Subject: meets the challenge in spades. Technical (Colour and light): This is good natural light from the looks ... and I love the DOF ... I am biased on selective desat and think it does work in some cases but it seems a little overkill in this shot ... To grow its vote?: I would have loved to have seen this in colour to see how that works ... this I think would make a huge difference to the shot. Summary: Good shooting .. you are overall improving all the time ... If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via the PM system. Cheers Kari', '2006-05-07 01:41:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(2388657, 323522, 41802, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>"Trinity Reflected" is a very interesting addition in the Window Framed challenge.  I really do like the shot, and I guess you had a different interpretation of the challenge which is always good in my opinion.<br/> <br/>The overall image is a great idea and I really like the frame being as full as you could fill it with the building.  I think you might have placed higher if you increased the colors either by the levels of the contrast.   This was a very natural looking shot, I read your comments and for not really meaning to take the shot it looks pretty good.  Also I understand that you were able to make it bigger because of that, but because you are pretty close I don''t think it hurt your score as much as it could of if the image were much smaller.<br/> <br/>I am very glad you took the time to enter this challenge and I look forward to your future challenges.</td>', '*Critique Club* "Trinity Reflected" is a very interesting addition in the Window Framed challenge.  I really do like the shot, and I guess you had a different interpretation of the challenge which is always good in my opinion. The overall image is a great idea and I really like the frame being as full as you could fill it with the building.  I think you might have placed higher if you increased the colors either by the levels of the contrast.   This was a very natural looking shot, I read your comments and for not really meaning to take the shot it looks pretty good.  Also I understand that you were able to make it bigger because of that, but because you are pretty close I don''t think it hurt your score as much as it could of if the image were much smaller. I am very glad you took the time to enter this challenge and I look forward to your future challenges.', '2006-05-07 01:43:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(2388659, 324200, 43434, '<td valign="top"><b><i>::: Critique Club :::</i></b> <br/> <br/>Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club.<br/> <br/><b>First Impression - the most important one:</b> <br/>Ok you already know from my previous comments i don''t think this meets the challenge, but I still think it is a lovely shot.<br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>The bird is nicely framed here .. <br/> <br/><b>Subject:</b> <br/>did not meet the challenge .. <br/> <br/><b>Technical (Colour and light):</b> <br/>natual works well here.  nice and sharp and a good DOF unless you want the window frame to be used in the shot.<br/> <br/><b>To grow its vote?:</b> <br/>Meet the challenge :) ... <br/> <br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>Go for it .. your portfolio really shows you are doing well ... I like out of the box pics :)<br/> <br/>If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via the PM system.<br/> <br/>Cheers<br/> <br/>Kari</td>', '::: Critique Club :::  Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club. First Impression - the most important one: Ok you already know from my previous comments i don''t think this meets the challenge, but I still think it is a lovely shot. Composition: The bird is nicely framed here ..  Subject: did not meet the challenge ..  Technical (Colour and light): natual works well here.  nice and sharp and a good DOF unless you want the window frame to be used in the shot. To grow its vote?: Meet the challenge :) ...  Summary: Go for it .. your portfolio really shows you are doing well ... I like out of the box pics :) If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via the PM system. Cheers Kari', '2006-05-07 01:45:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(2388676, 324631, 41802, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>"Admiring..." is an interesting twist on to the Window Framed challenge.<br/> <br/>One of the hardest things I have learned is that even if you have a good shot if voters do not feel the shot fit the category your score will tank.   I really think that is was has happened here.<br/> <br/>As for the photo itself.... I really like the idea and implementation.  The composition is prefect.  I love the reflection and it looks crystal clear (in the reflection specifically) from where I am sitting.  I would be curious to see the castle itself, it looks amazing.  The dof looks just right for a nice tight shot like this.  I do like the border that you included, it tends to balance out the closeness.  Overall this is a very nice shot, I think it may have done better in a different category.<br/> <br/>Keep up the good work!</td>', '*Critique Club* "Admiring..." is an interesting twist on to the Window Framed challenge. One of the hardest things I have learned is that even if you have a good shot if voters do not feel the shot fit the category your score will tank.   I really think that is was has happened here. As for the photo itself.... I really like the idea and implementation.  The composition is prefect.  I love the reflection and it looks crystal clear (in the reflection specifically) from where I am sitting.  I would be curious to see the castle itself, it looks amazing.  The dof looks just right for a nice tight shot like this.  I do like the border that you included, it tends to balance out the closeness.  Overall this is a very nice shot, I think it may have done better in a different category. Keep up the good work!', '2006-05-07 01:50:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(2388677, 324072, 43434, '<td valign="top"><b><i>::: Critique Club :::</i></b> <br/> <br/>Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club.<br/> <br/><b>First Impression - the most important one:</b> <br/>Interesting framing here .. a little soft on the focus ...<br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>I like that the boat is in the single frame here ... it works on that ... the angle of the pic also works to me.<br/> <br/><b>Subject:</b> <br/>meets the challenge .. I really hope this wasn''t really your bedroom .. cos no shot is worth getting pnuemonia.<br/> <br/><b>Technical (Colour and light):</b> <br/>I like the darkness it adds to the mood .. but the shot itself is soft and a little out of focus.<br/> <br/><b>To grow its vote?:</b> <br/>I think this did well ... it is a solid shot .. and nicely emotive .. the sky being blue may have added .1 but I think that is all ...<br/> <br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>Your work is a little like mine in consistency going through periods of fantastic and ok .. but never "bad" ... keep up the work towards the consistency and improvement.<br/> <br/>If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via the PM system.<br/> <br/>Cheers<br/> <br/>Kari</td>', '::: Critique Club :::  Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club. First Impression - the most important one: Interesting framing here .. a little soft on the focus ... Composition: I like that the boat is in the single frame here ... it works on that ... the angle of the pic also works to me. Subject: meets the challenge .. I really hope this wasn''t really your bedroom .. cos no shot is worth getting pnuemonia. Technical (Colour and light): I like the darkness it adds to the mood .. but the shot itself is soft and a little out of focus. To grow its vote?: I think this did well ... it is a solid shot .. and nicely emotive .. the sky being blue may have added .1 but I think that is all ... Summary: Your work is a little like mine in consistency going through periods of fantastic and ok .. but never "bad" ... keep up the work towards the consistency and improvement. If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via the PM system. Cheers Kari', '2006-05-07 01:51:01.000000', NULL, 0),
